    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Monotonic sequence** (near the `AUDIT` logger): a static `AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ`, incremented once per successful create so each event carries a strictly greater `seq`.\n\n2. **Event emission** (right after the existing audit line): \n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(ownerCreatedEvent(AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ.incrementAndGet(), owner));\n   ```\n   This is additive \u2014 the original human-readable audit line is untouched.\n\n3. **Two helpers**:\n   - `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` \u2014 returns the owner's *current* primary identifier. Today it returns `customerCode`; this is the single seam that the spec calls out, so when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only this accessor changes and the event automatically carries the memberId.\n   - `ownerCreatedEvent(seq, owner)` \u2014 renders the immutable JSON object `{\"seq\":\u2026,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"customerCode\":\u2026,\"membershipLevel\":\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, where the `customerCode` value is the primary identifier. All values are numeric or drawn from `[A-Z0-9-]`, so no JSON escaping is needed.\n\nEmitted output confirms the shape:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
